READY covered one layer stronger by builtin-curl-pipe-shell, so the new sandbox rule targets the real remaining gap (path-qualified/wrapped interpreter stage). Two PRE-EXISTING defects found and filed as TJ-GAP-066/-067 (aggregate MODIFY drops rule_id; sandboxed pipeline reconstruction drops the `|`).", "foreman_note": "Tick #284. Foreman-verified at 9fda86a, independent of the worker report: (a) own live probe, 35 vectors -> 15/15 block vectors BLOCK with the expected new rule id (incl. quoted + /dev/udp forms), 7/7 sandbox vectors MODIFY, 13/13 ALLOW pins ALLOW; (b) full suite 536 passed / 14 skipped (baseline 435/14); (c) plugin/test_packaging.py 8 passed (id-set + per-layer counts + RuleLoader pattern parity); (d) uvx ruff check . -> All checks passed!; (e) scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py totals block=26/26 sandbox=12/12 allow=10/10 total=48/48 OK (engine == YAML); (f) gitreins guard PASS 4/4; (g) CI run 35326981230 success on the content commit; 0 unpushed. KNOWN-STALE, deliberately deferred: YAML header prose '30 rules (12/8/10)' + README/quickstart counts are owned by DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-9. resolved_without_code: no.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": "PASS: each listed vector has a block/modify verdict + regression test; the allow-pins (ssh deploy cmd, git push, plain curl/wget) prove no fleet breakage.", "created_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "updated_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "blocked_since": null, "id": "TJ-GAP-058", "title": "[P1] Network egress rule class: reverse shells (/dev/tcp, nc -e, socat EXEC), upload-exfil (curl -T/--upload-file, wget --post-file), staged pipes", "detail": "2026-09-16 research identified the biggest uncovered class: nothing in the engine touches network egress. An agent can call home or ship data out. Vectors to cover (block the unambiguous, sandbox the dual-use): (1) reverse shells — bash /dev/tcp/HOST/PORT redirects, `bash -i >& /dev/tcp/...` classic, nc/ncat -e or -c shell attach, socat EXEC:'sh', pty,reverse; mkfifo + telnet/nc two-way plumbing; openssl s_client -connect piped to sh (unambiguous exfil/shell shapes only, not TLS diagnostics); (2) upload exfil — curl -T/--upload-file, --data-binary @large-path, wget --post-file, scp/rsync of suspicious whole-tree scope (rsync -a / to remote target); (3) staged pipes — curl host/script | sh is ALREADY covered (builtin-fetch-pipe); extend to wget -O- | sh, python -c urllib urlopen|exec shapes. DUAL-USE must NOT hard-block: plain `ssh host`, `scp file host:` are fleet-legit (deploys run on ssh) — give them action=modify (auto-sandbox) or leave allow + document; plain `curl url`, `wget url` stay ALLOW (downloads are normal); git push stays ALLOW. PASS: each listed vector has a block/modify verdict + regression test; the allow-pins (ssh deploy cmd, git push, plain curl/wget) prove no fleet breakage.", "judge_verdict": "PASS 5/5 (tier1 PASS + tier2 PASS, verdict 1e434618, record 3057b45e, COMPLETE)"}
 {"status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "primary_provider": "zai-glm-default", "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Bane 2026-09-17 asked how we track online escape research; this turns the canonical Unix catalog into a standing measurement instead of one-off probes. 478 binaries cannot all be blocked (vim/less/git are legit) — the harness makes the conscious allow-decisions VISIBLE and regression-guarded.", "capability_tags": ["verification", "research", "ci", "tests"], "worker_status": "pending", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": null, "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "created_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "updated_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "blocked_since": null, "id": "TJ-GAP-059", "title": "[P2] GTFOBins-sweep harness: machine-readable catalog -> per-function-class verdict matrix, coverage % tracked in CI", "detail": "Stop hand-picking vectors: build scripts/gtfobins-sweep that consumes a machine-readable GTFOBins dump (pwncat's gtfobins.json schema, MIT-licensed data pipeline — fetch at TEST time or vendor a snapshot WITHOUT license ambiguity; GTFOBins content is MIT, verify before vendoring) and generates, for each binary x function class (shell/file-read/file-write/library-load/sudo), the representative command from the catalog, runs it through intercept() verdict-only (NEVER executes), and emits a coverage matrix: blocked / modified(sandbox) / allowed per class. Record baseline numbers in the repo (coverage.md or test fixture) and fail CI only on REGRESSION (a class that was blocked becoming allowed), never on absolute coverage — the doctrine stays 'block the unambiguous, jail as backstop', so low coverage on benign binaries is