 {"status": "completed", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 3, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "primary_provider": "zai-glm-default", "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Turns the rules.d override mechanism (previously an incident) into a first-class feature with an explicit precedence and id-prefix contract, and gives niche policy (database abuse, k8s, CI-metadata) a home without bloating the default firewall for hosts that never touch those surfaces.", "capability_tags": ["architecture", "cli", "packaging", "security"], "worker_status": "completed", "dispatched_at": "2026-09-19T04:44:00+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-09-19T05:06:00+00:00", "attempts": 1, "exit_code": 0, "commit_hash": "a33adf1", "files_changed": 8, "lines_added": 1716, "lines_removed": 22, "guard_result": "PASS 4/4 (gitreins guard --full: secrets / lint / tests(full) / static_analysis; log .gitreins/logs/guard-20260919T050129.764467Z.log)", "ci_result": "success — run 35423185611 on a33adf19 (main)", "worker_summary": "glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm-default, one dispatch (~14 min), commit a33adf1 (+1716/-22, 8 files). install.sh gained POSIX flag parsing (--rule-pack repeatable, --unrule-pack, --list-rule-packs, -h/--help; unknown flag/name -> exit 2, nothing written) and the rules-target resolution became resolve_user_rules_dir(), shared by the default rules file and every pack (DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-8 scope rule unchanged). scripts/rule-pack-tool.py validates (schema + pack-<name>-* id namespace + collision against engine-derived builtin ids and already-installed rule files; fail-closed where the engine fails open) and lists packs. plugin/terminal_jail/rules/packs/db.yaml = first pack (2 block @950, 1 sandbox @650, ids pack-db-*; the wider catalogue stays TJ-GAP-062). 39 new tests (plugin/test_rule_packs.py, install cases in plugin/test_install.py). README + specs/cli.md + specs/interruptor.md pin the flags and the builtins < packs < user rules.d precedence contract.", "foreman_note": "Tick #294 foreman verification, independent of the worker: sh -n/dash -n clean; scratch-prefix install --rule-pack db wrote a BYTE-IDENTICAL terminal-jail-pack-db.yaml beside 00-builtins.yaml (cmp identical); --unrule-pack db removed only that file (seeded foreign file + 00-builtins.yaml survived, builtins unchanged by cmp); collision refusal rc=2 with \"collide with engine builtin ids\" and NO file written; schema-invalid pack rc=2, nothing written; unknown pack/flag rc=2; live intercept() probe with TERMINAL_JAIL_INTERRUPTOR_{,USER_}RULES_DIR pinned to scratch dirs: pack ABSENT -> allow/rule_id None for all three positives, pack INSTALLED -> block/pack-db-drop-database, block/pack-db-drop-table, modify/pack-db-dump-restore, pack REMOVED -> back to allow/None; suite 860 passed / 5 skipped (+39 vs the 821/5 baseline at 8e2230f); uvx ruff check . All checks passed; scripts/yaml-mirror-parity-probe.py 54/54 (35 block/9 sandbox/10 allow) -> ALL PROBES PASS (the pack is not loaded by default, correct); guard --full 4/4; tier-2 judge PASS (tier1+tier2, passed=true, 6/6 criteria, record .gitreins/history/2026-09-19/e3c161e3/verdict.json). Post-judge tree proof: sha256 of all 8 files == content commit a33adf1, no modified source file (tick #292 lesson applied). Named residuals carried in the row and in specs/interruptor.md 3.4: the collision oracle sees engine builtins + the resolved USER rules dir only (a root-managed /etc rules.d entry carrying a pack-* id is invisible to an unprivileged installer); packs are not packaged into a wheel (pyproject package-data still rules/*.yaml, installer reads the checkout); no --rule-pack run ever touched the live $HOME.", "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "created_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "updated_at": "2026-09-19T05:12:00+00:00", "blocked_since": null, "id": "TJ-GAP-061", "title": "[P1] Rule-pack system: opt-in curated rule sets (rules/packs/*.yaml) selectable at install/CLI time, explicit precedence contract", "detail": "Bane 2026-09-17: 'a way to enable extra rules that are not part of the main set'. Design: ship curated packs as rules/packs/<name>.yaml in-repo (our own content, MIT, no licensing exposure); install.sh gains --rule-pack <name> (repeatable) and --list-rule-packs; the standalone wrapper + bridge already merge user rules from ~/.config/terminal-jail/rules.d/*.yaml, so a pack install = writing rules.d/terminal-jail-pack-<name>.yaml — no new engine merge code needed. CONTRACTS to pin: (a) precedence — engine builtins < packs < user rules.d files, and a pack rule id NEVER overrides a builtin id (the 2026-09-16 shadowing incident proved same-id user copy silently overrides engine rules; packs must use prefixed ids like pack-db-*, collision = install error, not silent override); (b) schema validation at install time (bad pack = refuse, not skip); (c) uninstall path (--unrule-pack) that removes only that pack's file; (d) each pack ships its own test file exercising its rules through intercept(); (e) README lists packs with what they block and the false-positive stance. Main set stays lean by default — packs are opt-in per host. PASS: install --rule-pack db on a scratch prefix writes the pack file, engine loads it (bridge probe shows new verdicts), uninstall removes it, schema-invalid pack refused, suite green."}
 {"status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": "TJ-GAP-061", "blocks": null, "primary_model": "glm-5.3-flash", "primary_provider": "zai-glm-default", "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": "Concrete first consumer of the pack system, taken verbatim from Bane's 2026-09-17 example. Database abuse is a real agent failure mode (agent told to 'clean up' drops the wrong schema) and the fleet itself runs postgres/sqlite/duckdb, so the allow-pins protect OUR infra while the pack protects hosts where agents get DB clients.", "capability_tags": ["security", "database", "interruptor", "tests"], "worker_status": "pending", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": null, "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": null, "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 0, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "blocked_reason": null, "review_notes": null, "created_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "updated_at": "2026-09-16 22:48:06", "blocked_since": null, "id": "TJ-GAP-062", "title": "[P2] First rule pack 'db': database-destructive-ops (psql \\! escape, DROP DATABASE, mysql SHUTDOWN, redis CONFIG/MODULE, mongosh drop, data-dir rm)", "detail": "Bane's example class: 'stuff that could abuse a database'. Pack contents (all prefixed pack-db-*): (1) psql meta-shell escape — psql -c '\\! ...' / interactive \\! (arbitrary shell via the DB client); (2) SQL destruction literals on command line: DROP DATABASE, DROP SCHEMA CASCADE, TRUNCATE ... CASCADE (unqualified TRUNCATE stays out — too legit for maintenance), mysqladmin/sql DROP statements piped from shell; (3) mysqladmin shutdown / mariadb-admin shutdown; (4) redis-cli CONFIG SET dir/module tricks + MODULE LOAD (the redis RCE pattern), redis-cli FLUSHALL/FLUSHDB; (5) mongosh/mongo --eval dropDatabase/shutdown; (6) rm -rf on live data dirs: /var/lib/postgresql*, /var/lib/mysql*, /var/lib/mongodb*, /var/lib/redis*, *.duckdb targets (careful: DuckBrain's own .duckdb lives on this host — the rule must key on rm -rf + those paths, which is always an attack or a disaster, never routine); (7) pg_dump/mysqldump piped straight to a network target (dump | nc/curl -T - ftp://...) — exfil shape. LEGIT PINS (must stay allow/modify, prove with tests): plain psql -c 'SELECT ...', psql -f migration.sql, sqlite3 db 'INSERT ...' (our state.db/role.db live here), alembic/python -c ORM usage, pg_dump to local file, redis-cli GET/SET. Destructive-but-gray (single-table DROP, TRUNCATE one table) = action modify (auto-sandbox) not block, per doctrine. Ships with plugin/test_rule_pack_db.py. Depends on TJ-GAP-061 (pack loader)."}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-11", "title": "[dogfood:P1] Auto-sandbox (modify) dead-ends on DEGRADED hosts: the wrapper's bare-mode preflight exits 2 BEFORE executing bridge-prefixed commands", "detail": "Live at HEAD 186dc77: `./standalone/terminal-jail bash /tmp/x/evil.sh` prints '[terminal-jail] Modified: ... -> sandboxed' then 'terminal-jail: namespace creation failed (unshare exit 1); command not run — on unprivileged hosts try --user', rc=2, command never run. Same for `terminal-jail uv run pytest ...`. The bridge chose the legacy user-ns prefix `unshare --user --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c ...` (interruptor/userns.py:43 LEGACY_USER_FLAGS) — and IDENTICAL flags succeed via `terminal-jail --user echo` (rc=0, verified same session), so the prefix itself works. Root cause is ordering: standalone/terminal-jail:366 runs the bare-mode preflight probe and exits 2 at :370 before the already-prefixed detection at :386-387 ('bridge already prepended its own unshare prefix — run as-is') is ever reached. Net effect: all 8 auto-sandbox classes (make, pytest, go test, pip install, cargo, gcc, npm test, ./script.sh) are UNUSABLE end-to-end on this host class — the firewall picks isolation for you and the wrapper then refuses to run it. skills/terminal-jail-usage/SKILL.md pitfall 7 still claims 'the nested namespace works on this host (PID 1 inside)' — stale since at least the preflight reorder.", "priority": "P1", "source": "dogfood-cron", "reasoning": {"note": "dogfood cycle 2026-09-17 — verdict PROMISING-BUT-ROUGH (t2fs <5s, friction 5; live board re-verification pass)"}, "review_notes": "Fix: when the incoming command already carries a bridge prefix, skip or re-branch the bare preflight (probe with the prefix's own flags instead); add a DEGRADED-host end-to-end regression for action=modify. PASS: `terminal-jail bash script.sh` on a DEGRADED host executes sandboxed and returns the inner command's rc, or fails with an honest 'modify unavailable on this host' verdict — not a generic ", "ts": "2026-09-17T10:19:41.000Z", "worker_status": "done", "completed_at": "2026-09-18 20:56:03.000000", "updated_at": "2026-09-18 20:56:07", "commit_hash": "bd40d47", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "foreman_note": "Closed tick #290. Live proof: unshare backend + bridge modify -> INNER_RAN rc=7 (was rc=2 namespace failure at ef75ac9); stub-bridge uncreatable rewrite prefix -> honest modify-unavailable rc=2, inner never ran; explicit --user and block verdicts unchanged. Red-first: wrapper reverted to ef75ac9 gives 5 failed/1 passed on plugin/test_modify_preflight.py. Sibling defect QA-TERMINAL-JAIL-8 (subuid host test brittleness) is the same root cause and stays open.", "exit_code": "0", "files_changed": "[\"standalone/terminal-jail\",\"plugin/test_modify_preflight.py\",\"specs/cli.md\",\"README.md\",\"docs/quickstart.md\",\"docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md\",\"CHANGELOG.md\",\"skills/terminal-jail-usage/SKILL.md\"]", "lines_added": "456", "lines_removed": "13", "model_used": "glm-5.3-flash", "provider_used": "zai-glm-default", "attempts": "1"}
